Q: Upgrading phpMyAdmin to 4.3.4 A: <p>I also got similar issues when I upgraded phpmyadmin on my xampp to 4.4.15.3 version.</p>

<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/zh5DS.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/zh5DS.png" alt="screenshot"></a></p>

<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/kobPp.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/kobPp.png" alt="Errors screenshot"></a></p>

<p>To fix this I copied following values from <em>config.sample.inc.php</em> and moved to <em>config.inc.php</em></p>

<p>after /* Advanced phpMyAdmin features */ line</p>

<pre><code>    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['column_info'] = 'pma__column_info';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['recent'] = 'pma__recent';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['favorite'] = 'pma__favorite';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['table_uiprefs'] = 'pma__table_uiprefs';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['users'] = 'pma__users';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['usergroups'] = 'pma__usergroups';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['navigationhiding'] = 'pma__navigationhiding';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['savedsearches'] = 'pma__savedsearches';
    $cfg['Servers'][$i]['central_columns'] = 'pma__central_columns';
</code></pre>

<p>and restarted the mysql server.</p>

Q: Html text on button won&#39;t change colour A: <p>You have a clickable element <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> nested inside a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> element, which is also clickable. This is technically invalid HTML.</p>
<p>As for why your current HTML is styled the way it is? That's because the browser defines a default <code>color</code> for <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tags. Your current CSS uses the <code>.button</code> selector. The native color for the <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tag overrides the inherited color from the <code>.button</code> ancestor.</p>
<p>The easy fix is to simply remove the <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tag:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button class=&quot;button&quot;&gt;
    Home
&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If you need an additional element to apply styling, use a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> tag instead:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button class=&quot;button&quot;&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;Home&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> tag is semantically meaningless, and is perfectly valid to nest inside a clickable element, yet it can provide another element to apply styling to, if necessary.</p>
